  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday Night through Friday)\nIssued at 1052 PM CDT Fri Aug 28 2026\n\nThe predominant upper flow pattern over the CONUS next week will\nfeature broad upper ridging over the central and eastern CONUS, \nwith troughing over the Northeast and the Pacific Northwest. \nBoundaries that could focus storms will stay well away from the \narea in this pattern. There is a hint of some isolated shower or\nstorm activity in the terrain of western AR from Tuesday onward,\nbut the signal is weak and thus confidence does not merit \nintroducing PoPs at this point. The grand ensemble mean has \npositive 500mb height anomalies over the region clear through the\nfirst week of September, including the Labor Day Weekend. \nTemperature-wise, Sunday looks to be the hottest day of the \nforecast, with temps dialing back slightly and holding there \n(around 100F) for most of next week. Heat headlines will likely be\nneeded for portions of the area Sunday and in the days following.\nHot and windy conditions from Sunday into next week will bring \nfire weather concerns each day at least locally as the drought \nworsens.\n\nThe longer range outlook for week 2 from CPC, taking us through \nSeptember 11th, continues to favor above average temps and below\naverage precip.\n\nLacy",
